=== 1. -c string: trap fires when the string ends
hi
bye
rc=0
=== 2. exit N: $? in the trap is N and the shell exits with N
bye 3
rc=3
=== 3. exit inside the trap overrides; bare exit keeps the status
in-trap
rc=7
rc=3
one
rc=0
=== 4. set -e exit runs the trap
a
cleanup 1
rc=1
=== 5. exit from a function
trap 4
rc=4
=== 6. the latest trap wins; trap - and trap '' disable it
second
none
ignored
z
zero
=== 7. the trap sees the final state and positionals
late a1 n1
trap -- 'trap -p' EXIT
=== 8. script file
child
child-bye 6
rc=6
=== 9. subshells keep their own EXIT trap
sub
sub2
sub-bye
sub rc=9
=== 10. command substitution runs its own trap into the capture
x=[cs
cs-bye]
y=[plain]
=== 11. exec replaces the shell: no trap
replaced
rc=0
rc=1
=== 12. stdout redirected away, trap output on stderr
bye
=== end (parent trap follows)
parent-bye
